    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d642">

                <pb facs="0556" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.0.0/488a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Ambassador Page.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 22, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>178. Department does not appear to be in cable communication with Monrovia.
                    Forward following message to American Minister there:</p>
                <p>“Telegraph briefly effect European war is having on conditions in Liberia.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
